README find_fid

This script will take spot and orientate it in front of a fiducial at a set distnace

It uses graph nav first to find the fiducial and get it within a large margin of error
Then use command client to get within a few centimeters of where it is supposed to be


fine_align:

1. Take new picture of the fiducial
2. Transform from fiducial frame to robot ODOM frame
3. Transform from current frame to goal frame
4. Flatten, get rid of z axis
5. 
Odom frame override: use get_a_tform_b(..., ODOM_FRAME_NAME, tag_frame_name), by bypassing seed frame, strip out SLAM drift. 
SE(2) Flattening: Convert 3D SE(3) matrix into 2D SE(2) matrix. If fiducial is cooked, SE(3) will try to rotate to match fiducials rotation. Flattening makes sure spot is level. 
Feedback loop: unlike graph nav, RobotCommandClient STATUS_AT_GOAL means the robot has mechanically settled its footprint exactly on the requested coordinate, within the margin of error(1-2 cm)

world_object_client = robot.ensure_client(WorldObjectClient.default_service_name) pass the class attribute instead of the raw string

Trajectory commands bypass the graphnav mirco planner